      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "FALSIFIABILITY",
      "narration_text": "Here's the difference I'd push for. The easy way bolts an M C P server on with its own access rules and lets it write content. The way I'd argue for builds on two point oh: the same access check every book already uses, read-only until reviewed, and piloted in isolation first. An A I interface should inherit the human gates, not route around them.",
